From cf5b11f266731fcf8d93f78c195d4c6817ed88fb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sjcsf <346224915+llsf2020@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 16/16] FreeChat: strict mode covers SSO, OAuth and QR logins

Those logins stored the credentials and a pickle key, then started the
session from storage, so a strict session left an access token on disk
until the page was closed (or until the next start, if the sign-out on
close never ran). In strict mode they now hold the credentials in memory
and restoreSessionFromStorage starts the session from them. Refreshed
tokens are not written to storage either.
---
 apps/web/src/Lifecycle.ts                | 20 +++++++++++++++
 apps/web/src/freechat/strictMode.test.ts | 32 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 apps/web/src/freechat/strictMode.ts      | 21 ++++++++++++++++
 apps/web/src/utils/createMatrixClient.ts |  5 +++-
 4 files changed, 77 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

